ink><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-are-turning-seawater-into-a-blood-test-that-could-reveal-coral-reef-damage-before-it-becomes-visible/articleshow/132682241.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-are-turning-seawater-into-a-blood-test-that-could-reveal-coral-reef-damage-before-it-becomes-visible/articleshow/132682241.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-28T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132682278,imgsize-297774.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Will Smith once used this $2.5 million, 1,200-square-foot motorhome on film sets; the two-storey vehicle is now a luxury stay near Austin: Why it remains so special]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132682994.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Will Smith's custom-built luxury motorhome, 'The Heat,' is now available for rent. This impressive 53-foot double-decker RV offers extensive living space and advanced features. It previously served Smith during major film productions like 'Ali' and 'Suicide Squad.' The motorhome now anchors a glamping resort outside Austin, Texas. Guests can experience a taste of Hollywood luxury at a significantly reduced price.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/will-smith-once-used-this-2-5-million-1200-square-foot-motorhome-on-film-sets-the-two-storey-vehicle-is-now-a-luxury-stay-near-austin-why-it-remains-so-special/articleshow/132682994.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/will-smith-once-used-this-2-5-million-1200-square-foot-motorhome-on-film-sets-the-two-storey-vehicle-is-now-a-luxury-stay-near-austin-why-it-remains-so-special/articleshow/132682994.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-28T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132683121,imgsize-94573.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists capture first wild footage of rare Arctic squid with its eggs]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132683258.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Scientists documented a rare Arctic bobtail squid guarding its eggs in Northeast Greenland.  This marks the first confirmed in situ record of Rossia moelleri in its natural habitat.  The observation occurred in the world's largest national park, a remote Arctic fjord.  This finding fills a gap in understanding Arctic cephalopods and their reproduction.  It provides a baseline for tracking marine life in a rapidly warming Arctic region.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-filmed-this-rare-arctic-squid-in-the-wild-for-the-first-time-guarding-its-eggs-in-sub-zero-water-inside-the-worlds-largest-national-park/articleshow/132683258.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-filmed-this-rare-arctic-squid-in-the-wild-for-the-first-time-guarding-its-eggs-in-sub-zero-water-inside-the-worlds-largest-national-park/articleshow/132683258.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-28T17:06:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132683567,imgsize-220899.cms"/></item></channel></rss>